From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: glacier <hyouga.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 02:42:26 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Gate the checkIfActive timer behind verbose timings

SpigotTimings.checkIfActiveTimer wraps ActivationRange.checkIfActive, which runs
once per entity per tick and measures a handful of field reads, an int modulo and
one chunk lookup. The timer costs more than the work it times.

Every other per-item timer in the same file is already gated - "## tickEntity",
"## tickTileEntity", "## tickEntity - <type>", "## Scheduled Block: <name>" - and
a name beginning with ## is only enabled when timings.verbose is set. This one was
not gated, so it ran on every server with timings on at all, which is the default.

Measured with JFR on a fixed route, all runs with timings enabled and verbose off,
so the only difference is this line:

                         without    with
  ActivationRange.checkIfActive   2.20%  ->  0.88% of the server thread
  TimingHandler.addDiff           3.43%  ->  2.05%

For reference the same route with the stock config (verbose on) spends 5.81% of
the server thread inside TimingHandler, and with timings switched off entirely
checkIfActive costs 1.32% - so with this change a verbose-off server pays less for
the check than the timer alone used to cost.

This changes what /timings reports only for operators who have set
timings.verbose to false, which is the setting that already drops the per-entity
and per-tile-entity breakdowns. The default, timings.verbose = true, reports
exactly what it did before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/src/main/java/co/aikar/timings/SpigotTimings.java b/src/main/java/co/aikar/timings/SpigotTimings.java
index 2a87b088f57adecf78ba0b7ea4c9358d805075f4..f64ebd2513f45763229bd79b951da5e48f39d3db 100644
--- a/src/main/java/co/aikar/timings/SpigotTimings.java
+++ b/src/main/java/co/aikar/timings/SpigotTimings.java
@@ -27,7 +27,13 @@ public final class SpigotTimings {
     public static final Timing playerCommandTimer = Timings.ofSafe("playerCommand");
 
     public static final Timing entityActivationCheckTimer = Timings.ofSafe("entityActivationCheck");
-    public static final Timing checkIfActiveTimer = Timings.ofSafe("checkIfActive");
+    // Athena - mark this one verbose, the way every other per-entity timer in this file already
+    // is. It runs once per entity per tick, and what it measures is a handful of field reads, an
+    // int modulo and one chunk lookup - a JFR capture put ActivationRange.checkIfActive at 3.07%
+    // of the server thread with timings on and 1.32% with them off, so the timer cost more than
+    // half of what was attributed to the method it was timing. "## tickEntity" and
+    // "## tickTileEntity" next to it are gated for exactly this reason; this one was not.
+    public static final Timing checkIfActiveTimer = Timings.ofSafe("## checkIfActive");
 
     public static final Timing antiXrayUpdateTimer = Timings.ofSafe("anti-xray - update");
     public static final Timing antiXrayObfuscateTimer = Timings.ofSafe("anti-xray - obfuscate");
